  "source": {
    "generator": null,
    "notes": "European arithmetic-basket call on N=3 equicorrelated assets, priced by exact-terminal Monte Carlo. The shocks are correlated via the native `correlations` field: build_corr_groups assembles the NxN correlation matrix, Cholesky-factors it, and the Gaussian copula on normal marginals reproduces the linear shock correlation exactly. The arithmetic basket (sum of lognormals) has no closed form; the geometric basket (a lognormal) does and is a ~0.997-correlated control variate with a live closed-form mean. Validation: geometric MC == closed form; arithmetic > geometric (AM-GM); the control cuts variance ~12x. Generalizes the two-asset spread example (Cholesky/Margrabe) to N assets. See BASKET_OPTION_EXAMPLE.md."
  },
